card.statement:
A commutative algebra $A$ in the braided category $\cC(\h,\Omega)$, which has a non-degenerate multiplicative bilinear form and has trivial subalgebra of invariants $A^\h=k$, has a form $k[\gl,\alpha]$, where $\gl$ is a subgroup of $\h$ such that the restriction of the form on $\gl$ is integer and even

$$(x,y)\in\Z,\quad (x,x)\in 2\Z,\quad x,y\in\gl.$$

The cohomology class of the cocycle $\alpha$ (and hence the isomorphism class of $k[\gl,\alpha]$) is uniquely defined by the condition:

\begin{equation}
\frac{\alpha(x,y)}{\alpha(y,x)} = e^{\pi i(x,y)}.
\end{equation}
